[Term]
id: CL:4030004
name: thymic nurse cell
def: "A large epithelial cell found in the thymus. This cell type may internalize thymocytes through extensions of plasma membrane. The cell surface and cytoplasmic vacuoles of a thymic nurse cell express MHC Class I and MHC Class II antigens. The interaction of these antigens with a developing thymocyte determines whether the thymocyte undergoes positive or negative selection." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thymic_nurse_cell] {http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473"}
is_a: CL:0002293 ! epithelial cell of thymus
relationship: dc-contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1773-2692
property_value: dcterms-date 2022-02-18T12:43:20Z xsd:dateTime

