creation_date: 2011-01-17T11:13:53Z

[Term]
id: GO:0072539
name: T-helper 17 cell differentiation
namespace: biological_process
def: "The process in which a relatively unspecialized T cell acquires the specialized features of a T-helper 17 (Th17) cell. A Th17 cell is a CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell with the phenotype RORgamma-t-positive that produces IL-17." [CL:0000899, GOC:BHF, GOC:ebc]
comment: Note that immunologists typically use the word 'development' to refer to cells of B or T cell lineages undergoing the process that GO describes as 'cell differentiation'.
