name: interstitial fluid
namespace: uberon
def: "Interstitial fluid is a bodily fluid consisting of a solution which bathes and surrounds the cells of multicellular animals. It is the main component of the extracellular fluid, which also includes plasma and transcellular fluid." [Wikipedia:Interstitial_fluid]
