property_value: depicted_by http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Human_ovarian_follicle.jpg xsd:anyURI
property_value: depicted_by https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Primary_follicle-4.JPG xsd:anyURI
property_value: editor_note "TODO - align subtypes based on staging, which is taxon-specific" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "Oocyte development of zebrafish has been divided into five stages based on morphological criteria and on physiological and biochemical events. Stage I follicles (less than 140 microns) are primary growth stage, stage II follicles (140-340 microns) are cortical alveolus stage, stage III (340-690 microns) are vitellogenesis, stage IV (690-730 microns) are oocyte maturation, and stage V follicles are matured egg. Selman et al, 1993.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0001110", ontology="TAO", source="ZFIN:curator"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000003 "Examination of different vertebrate species shows that the adult gonad is remarkably similar in its morphology across different phylogenetic classes. Surprisingly, however, the cellular and molecular programs employed to create similar organs are not evolutionarily conserved.[uncertain][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001536", ontology="VHOG", source="DOI:10.1146/annurev.cellbio.042308.13350 DeFalco T, Capel B, Gonad morphogenesis in vertebrates: divergent means to a convergent end. Annual review of cell and developmental biology (2009)", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "These structures are periodically initiated to grow and develop, culminating in ovulation of usually a single competent oocyte in humans. These eggs/ova are only developed once every menstrual cycle (e.g. once a month in humans)" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000009 "The somatic cell component of the follicle produces hormones important for oocyte development and proper endocrine function" xsd:string

