property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "in aves, stromal mesenchymal cells may migrate to the iris and become skeletal" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "The muscle cells of the iris are smooth muscle in mammals and amphibians, but are striated muscle in birds and reptiles. Many fish have neither, and, as a result, their irides are unable to dilate and contract, so that the pupil always remains of a fixed size[Romer, via WP]" xsd:string

