[Term]
id: UBERON:0001959
name: white pulp of spleen
namespace: uberon
def: "The parenchymatous tissue of the spleen that surrounds splenic blood vessels, consists of compact masses of lymphatic cells and is where foreign material removed from the blood is used to initiate an immune reaction that results in the production of antibodies." [MGI:csmith, MP:0002357]
