relationship: present_in_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 ! Homo sapiens
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "in the mouse, the lobes of the thymus are not subdivided into lobules but only in the central medulla and a peripheral cortex (i.e. there is no distinct sublobulation). In humans, the two thymus lobes are composed of many lobules of various sizes which contain follicles, each comprising a medulla and a cortex. in the rat, the thymus is partially subdivided into lobules separated by thin bands of connective tissue which are continuous with the thin connective tissue capsule.[MP]" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000010 "Lymphocytes, reticular cells and macrophages are found in the lobules" xsd:string

