relationship: adjacent_to UBERON:0003842 ! neural tube lumen
relationship: bounding_layer_of UBERON:0001049 ! neural tube
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001049 ! neural tube
property_value: UBPROP:0000011 "As the cells adjacent to the lumen continue to divide, the migrating cells form a second layer around the original neural tube. This layer becomes progressively thicker as more cells are added to it from the germinal neuroepithelium. This new layer is called the mantle (or intermediate) zone, and the germinal epithelium is now called the ventricular zone (and, later, the ependyma)[NCBIBook:NBK10047]" xsd:string

