[Term]
id: UBERON:0004179
name: prostate glandular acinus
namespace: uberon
def: "A saclike structure of the prostate gland, comprised of at least three cell layers: an innermost layer of secretory columnar luminal epithelium, a middle layer of squamous basal epithelium that also contains neuroendocrine cells, transit amplifying cells, and stem cells, and an outer layer of smooth muscle intermixed with other stromal cells." [GO:0060525, PMID:18977204]
synonym: "prostatic acinus" EXACT [FMA:66808]
synonym: "prostatic follicle" EXACT [FMA:66808]
xref: FMA:66808
