relationship: develops_from UBERON:0009843 {source="PMID:18977204"} ! prostate epithelial cord
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000428 {source="GO"} ! prostate epithelium
property_value: editor_note "the muscle layer is implicitly treated as outside the acinus" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000011 "Concurrent with branching morphogenesis, the solid cords of epithelium formed by budding arborize and differentiate postnatally into glandular acin. The basic prostate architecture is established by puberty and acquires secretory function thereafter[PMID:18977204]" xsd:string

