[Term]
id: UBERON:0007639
name: hippocampus alveus
namespace: uberon
def: "Regional part of fornix consisting of a thin layer of white matter on the surface of the hippocampal formation, bordering the wall of the lateral ventricle and composed of white, myelinated fibers. The alveus arises from cell bodies in the subiculum and hippocampus, and eventually merges with the fimbria of the hippocampus. The fimbria goes on to become the fornix (MM: 2006-10-26)." [BIRNLEX:1510]
synonym: "alveus" EXACT [BIRNLEX:1510]
