[Term]
id: UBERON:0007722
name: interphalangeal joint of manus
namespace: uberon
def: "The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): 'proximal interphalangeal joints' (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges 'distal interphalangeal joints' (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes." [Wikipedia:Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
subset: pheno_slim
