[Term]
id: UBERON:0013631
name: sesamoid element
namespace: uberon
def: "Ossicle that develops within bands of dense, regular connective tissue (e.g., tendons and ligaments). Sesamoids are generally located proximate to a bony prominence, over which the dense regular connective tissue wraps, and/or a joint or articulation." [PSPUB:0000169, VSAO:0000137]
comment: Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.
synonym: "sesamoid" EXACT [VSAO:0000137]
xref: VSAO:0000137
is_a: UBERON:0010911 {source="VSAO"} ! ossicle
relationship: develops_in UBERON:0007846 {source="VSAO"} ! dense regular connective tissue
